  "aesops-fables": "Originating in ancient Greece in the sixth century BCE, these parables use animal archetypes to illuminate everyday virtues such as humility, perseverance, and modesty.",
  "grimm-fairy-tales": "Folk stories documented by Jacob and Wilhelm Grimm in nineteenth-century Germany, celebrating the resilience of the humble, the wonder of generosity, and the beauty of keeping promises.",
  "hans-christian-andersen": "Hans Christian Andersen of Denmark elevated the fairy tale into high poetic art, exploring the emotional landscape of belonging, courage, and discovering inner beauty.",
